37067 17592186576411 false] [17592186259667 1071 "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=v-2u,\\,y=u+3v-1.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139537067 17592186576411 true] [17592186259667 1071 "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=v-2u,\\,y=u+3v-1.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **II.** $det(A)=-7$\n- **III.** The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" 13194139537067 17592186576411 false] [17592186259667 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is false. Notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}v-2u \\\\ u+3v-1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2u+v \\\\ u+3v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- Statement $det(A)=-7$ is true. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}=(-2)\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 1=-7.\n$$\n\n- Statement “The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving” is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the a